x/31px nyt-cheltenham,georgia,serif;margin:0 0 10px"><span>They said it cou=
ldn=E2=80=99t be moved</span></h2><p style=3D"display:block;color:#333;font=
:400 18.5px/26px georgia,serif;margin:0 0 10px"><span>by Alex Marshall</spa=
n></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0=
 15px"><span>When Emmanuel Macron of France first announced he=E2=80=99d lo=
an the Bayeux Tapestry to Britain, in 2018, I had a thought: That isn=E2=80=
=99t going to happen.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,s=
erif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Napoleon might once have shifted the=
 embroidery, which depicts the Norman invasion of Britain, from its home in=
 Bayeux, along bumpy roads to the Louvre in Paris. But in 1803, who was goi=
ng to argue with him=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia=
,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The Nazis also managed to shift th=
e tapestry around France =E2=80=94 ultimately hoping to steal it away to Ge=
rmany =E2=80=94 but few were going to resist them, either.</span></p><p sty=
le=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span=
>In 2018, Macron didn=E2=80=99t have the power of Napoleon, or the Nazis, a=
nd I thought he would struggle to overcome objections from the tapestry=E2=
=80=99s conservators, who said the tapestry was too fragile to leave its ho=
metown, let alone travel to Britain, where the embroidery was made.</span><=
/p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15=
px"><span>I was wrong. Eight years later, the tapestry is in the British Mu=
seum in London, the centerpiece of the most eagerly anticipated museum show=
 of the year, which opened yesterday and runs through July 11.</span></p><p=
 style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><=
span>The artifact=E2=80=99s high-security move proves that conservation sci=
ence has developed to the point where an object once thought immovable can =
cross borders. And that raises an intriguing question: If it=E2=80=99s now =
safe to move the tapestry, surely it=E2=80=99s safe to shift other supposed=
ly immovable priceless objects, too=3F</span></p><table border=3D"0" cellpa=
dding=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" style=3D"width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style=3D"=
