"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">16,445 wrinkles, 9,646 holes and 30 tears=
</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margi=
n:0 0 15px"><span>The Bayeux Tapestry is not a sturdy object. A 2020 study =
found it had 16,445 wrinkles, 9,646 holes and 30 tears, among other damage.=
 After Macron=E2=80=99s 2018 announcement, numerous conservators expressed =
their horror.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;col=
or:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>So what changed=3F The conservators I spoke =
to said a main difference was that they could now work with scientists and =
engineers to model the vibrations that might occur during transport, then d=
evelop methods to limit them. And in this case, they had the financial back=
ing to do such work properly.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px g=
eorgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>For its move to Britain, abo=
ut 100 technicians carefully put the tapestry into a crate, then a climate-=
controlled case suspended in a spring-mounted cage. The huge springs surrou=
nding that cage are sometimes used in earthquake zones, and have in recent =
years been used to move other fragile artworks including valuable pastels, =
sculptures and paintings.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georg=
ia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The technology isn=E2=80=99t per=
fect. Thalia Bajon-Bouzid, one of the tapestry=E2=80=99s conservators, said=
 in an email last week that the tapestry arrived in Britain with two thread=
 breaks, a few millimeters long. Still, she said, there was =E2=80=9Cno maj=
or visible damage.=E2=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px geo=
rgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Should a museum want to move a=
 supposedly-immovable masterpiece, there is now more evidence that this is =
possible. It also has more evidence that doing so can reap huge rewards.</s=
pan></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0=
 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">The return of the blockbuster exhi=
bition=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#=
333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The strange thing about the British Museum exhib=
